<section
        id="people"
        class="section wrap people-section"
        aria-labelledby="people-title"
      >
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">03 / People & paths</p>
            <h2>A few people worth <em>meeting.</em></h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            Different lenses. A useful way in.<br />No one has the whole map.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="people-grid">
          <article class="person">
            <div class="person-top">
              <span class="person-monogram apricot" aria-hidden="true">il.</span
              ><span class="eyebrow">Somatic education</span>
            </div>
            <h3>Irene Lyon</h3>
            <p>A way into sensory awareness and everyday somatic learning.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="https://irenelyon.com/free-resources/"
              >Explore her public resources ↗</a
            >
            <details>
              <summary>Know before you go</summary>
              <p>
                Educational work blending several approaches. Course claims are
                not the same as independent clinical evidence; some resources
                require email signup.
              </p>
            </details>
          </article>
          <article class="person">
            <div class="person-top">
              <span class="person-monogram lilac" aria-hidden="true">jh.</span
              ><span class="eyebrow">Emotional inquiry</span>
            </div>
            <h3>Joe Hudson</h3>
            <p>
              Curiosity about feelings, relationships, and the fear of being
              seen.
            </p>
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="https://www.artofaccomplishment.com/podcast/whats-beneath-your-fear-of-being-seen---coaching-with-joe"
              >Listen to a coaching conversation ↗</a
            >
            <details>
              <summary>Know before you go</summary>
              <p>
                Coaching and personal development, rather than a validated PTSD
                treatment. An invitation to feel more won’t fit every moment.
              </p>
            </details>
          </article>
          <article class="person">
            <div class="person-top">
              <span class="person-monogram sage" aria-hidden="true">jm.</span
              ><span class="eyebrow">Practical learning</span>
            </div>
            <h3>Jonny Miller</h3>
            <p>
              A structured vocabulary for stress, noticing, and experimentation.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link" href="https://www.nsmastery.com/topics"
              >Browse the public topic library ↗</a
            >
            <details>
              <summary>Know before you go</summary>
              <p>
                Nervous System Mastery is an educational program with paid
                offerings. Its “mastery” framing is a teaching approach, not a
                clinical outcome guarantee.
              </p>
            </details>
          </article>
          <article class="person">
            <div class="person-top">
              <span class="person-monogram butter" aria-hidden="true">bk.</span
              ><span class="eyebrow">Trauma research</span>
            </div>
            <h3>Bessel van der Kolk</h3>
            <p>
              Background on trauma, embodiment, and the research behind the
              conversation.
            </p>
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="https://traumaresearchfoundation.org/resources/"
              >Visit the research foundation ↗</a
            >
            <details>
              <summary>Know before you go</summary>
              <p>
                Some material is intense or intended for professionals. Evidence
                varies by intervention; a prominent author’s interest is not
                proof that a method works.
              </p>
            </details>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="section-footnote">
          A starting shelf, not a ranking or endorsement. Different resources suit different people; there’s no need to sign up for anything to begin.
        </p>
      </section>
